    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "‘Cúl na dTonn’ – Back of the Waves, Carrickbrack Road, Sutton, Dublin 13\r\n\r\n‘Cúl na dTonn’, meaning Back of the Waves, is a beautifully positioned family home on Carrickbrack Road, just off the ever-popular Strand Road in Sutton. With spectacular sea views and coastal and hill walks quite literally on your doorstep, this is a location that truly speaks for itself.\r\n\r\nOccupying a large, private, south-facing site with mature gardens to both front and rear, this substantial detached bungalow, while now in need of modernisation, presents a rare and exciting opportunity to create a magnificent family home in one of Dublin’s most sought-after coastal settings, there is also obvious potential to develop the site further subject to planning permission. \r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 2,352 sq. ft. / 218 sq. m., the well-proportioned accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming porch leading to a generous reception hallway. To the right lies a spacious kitchen with adjoining utility area and access to the garage. To the rear of the property is a bright open-plan dining and family room, along with a formal lounge featuring patio doors opening onto the wonderfully private and sun-drenched rear garden.\r\n\r\nThe bedroom accommodation is located to the left-hand side of the house and includes four generously sized bedrooms, a main ensuite, and a family bathroom. A large, partially converted attic room offers further potential for additional living space, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property is surrounded by expansive lawns bordered by mature hedgerows, ensuring exceptional privacy. The sunny rear garden boasts a substantial patio area and a swimming pool, ideal for outdoor entertaining and family enjoyment.\r\n\r\nThe location is second to none — just moments from excellent schools, sports clubs, Sutton Cross, and the DART, while the renowned coastal and hill walks of the Howth Peninsula are close by.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the exceptional potential and unrivalled setting this fine home has to offer."
